apple-delicious,apple,fruit-apple,Delicious,Malus domestica Borkh.,Dessert,"An American apple discovered in about 1880 growing as a shoot from a rootstock by J. Hiatt, near Peru, Iowa. It was introduced by Stark Brothers in 1895. Fruits have very firm, very sweet, juicy flesh with a highly aromatic flavour. Skin is very tough. Fruits have much better flavour when grown in climates with good temperature and light conditions.",Cervena prevazhodna|Delicious rosso|Hawkeye|Piros Delicious|Prevoshodnoe krasnoe|Red Delicious|Stark Delicious,Not currently held in the National Fruit Collection. Father to: Fuji Kidd's Orange Red Fukunishiki Orleans Medina Jonadel Empire Chieftain Regent Legana Kinrei Sweet Delicious Murasaki New Fuji Sports: Idaho Delicious Oregon Spur Starkspur Supreme Richared Delicious Starking Starkrimson Delicious Wellspur Delicious,False,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=1524&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),1524,,05-12,05-20,,Mid October,20,,,,,,,,,,,,medium,Truncate conical,strong,,Green yellow,,Red,striped,,crisp,Cream,58.00 mm,64.00 mm,firm,,
apple-golden-delicious,apple,fruit-apple,Golden Delicious,Malus domestica Borkh.,Dessert,"A chance seedling found in 1890 by A.H. Mullins, Clay County, West Virginia, USA. It was introduced in 1914 by Stark Brothers. Fruits have crisp, sweet, juicy flesh with a good aromatic flavour.",Arany delicious|Delicios auriu|Stark Golden Delicious|Yellow Delicious|Zlatna prevazhodna|Zolotoe prevoshodnoe,Material available from the National Fruit Collection. Mother to: Telstar Freyberg Korei Golden Melon Redgold Shinsei Mutsu Jonagold Odin Skinlite Magnolia Gold Sungold Ozark Gold Arlet Elstar Dorsett Golden Dukat Spur Sinta Criterion Kinrei Dukat Jonagored Supra Goro Goldjon Honeygold Priolov Delises Tsugaru Chehalis Cloden Nugget Charden Kougetsu Father to: Imperial Gala Spencer Ivette Shin Indo Horei Spigold Rubin Hatsuaki Gala Greensleeves Summerland Ingol Sports: Golden Delicious Horst No.2 Doud Golden Delicious Starkspur Golden Delicious Golden Auvilspur Lysgolden Clear Gold Goldensheen Goldspur Courtagold Ed Gould Golden Elbee Golden Morspur Lemon Pippin Merrigold Penco Smoothee Testerspur Golden Delicious,True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=2335&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),2335,,05-11,05-19,,Late October,20,,,,,,,,,,,,medium,Globose conical,weak-medium,medium,Yellow,,Orange,,low,crisp,Yellowish,67.00 mm,70.00 mm,,,
apple-granny-smith,apple,fruit-apple,Granny Smith,Malus domestica Borkh.,Dessert,"Raised by Mrs Thomas Smith, Ryde, New South Wales, Australia. Trees were known to be fruiting in 1868. Mrs Smith was born in Peasmarsh, Sussex in 1800 and emigrated to Australia in 1838. Fruits have firm, rather coarse-textured, juicy flesh with a subacid and refreshing flavour.",,Material available from the National Fruit Collection.,True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=2439&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),2439,,05-10,05-18,,Mid October,20,,,,,,,,,,,,large,Globose conical,weak,weak-medium,Whitish green,very low,Red,mottled/washed out,low,crisp,Greenish,69.58 mm,72.14 mm,firm-very firm,,
