apple-mcintosh,apple,fruit-apple,McIntosh,Malus domestica Borkh.,Dessert,"Discovered in 1796 by John McIntosh near Dundela, Dundas County, Ontario, Canada. Propagated by Allan McIntosh. It was introduced and named in about 1870. Fruits have white, rather soft, fine-textured, very juicy flesh with a sweet, pleasant vinous flavou",M'Intosh|Mac Intosh|Mac Intosh Red|Mac-Intosh|Mac-Intosh Red|MacIntosh|MacIntosh Red|Mackintosh|Mackintosh Red|Makintos|Mc Intosh|Mc-Intosh Red|Mc. I. Red|Mc.Intosh Red|McIntosh Red|Mek-Intosh|Mekintos,Material available from the National Fruit Collection. Material held in Tidnor Wood National Collection® of Malus (Cider making) Material held in the Marcher Apple Network collections (Tredomen),True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=3874&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),3874,,05-07,05-14,,Mid September,20,,,,,,,,,,,,large,Flat globose,weak-medium,weak-medium,Whitish yellow,medium,Red,striped/solid flush,low,crisp,White,59.83 mm,71.95 mm,soft,,
apple-cortland,apple,fruit-apple,Cortland,Malus domestica Borkh.,Dessert,"Raised in 1898 by S.A. Beach at New York State Agricultural Experiment Station, Geneva, USA. Fruits have moderately juicy, slightly coarse-textured flesh with a sweet, refreshing flavour. Skin is tough.",Cartland|Courtland|Courtlandt,Material available from the National Fruit Collection.,True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=1291&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),1291,,05-09,05-16,,Early October,20,,,,,,,,,,,,large,Broad globose conical,weak-medium,,Green yellow,high,Red,striped,very low,,,59.00 mm,75.00 mm,,,
apple-empire,apple,fruit-apple,Empire,Malus domestica Borkh.,Dessert,"Raised in 1945 at New York State Agricultural Experiment Station, Geneva, New York. It was named and introduced in 1966. Fruits have crisp flesh with a subacid and aromatic flavour.",,Material available from the National Fruit Collection.,True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=1868&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),1868,,05-09,05-16,,Mid October,20,,,,,,,,,,,,medium-large,Flat globose,very weak,,,very high,Red,striped,,crisp,Cream,,,,,
apple-jonathan,apple,fruit-apple,Jonathan,Malus domestica Borkh.,Dessert,"Originated on the farm of Philip Rick, Woodstock, Ulster County, New York, USA. It was first described in 1826 by Judge Buel who named the apple after Jonathan Hasbrouck. Fruits have soft, fine-textured, fairly juicy flesh with a sweet and fairly pleasant flavour.",Djonathan|Dzhonatan|Dzonetn|Esopus Spitzenberg (New)|Johnathan|King Philip|King Philipp|Philip Rick|Philipp Rick|Pomme Jonathan|Ulster|Ulster Seedling,Material available from the National Fruit Collection. Material held in Tidnor Wood National Collection® of Malus (Cider making),True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=3077&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),3077,,05-12,05-15,,Early October,20,,,,,,,,,,,,medium,Globose conical,weak,medium,Yellow,,Red,solid flush,low,,White,,,firm,,
apple-rome-beauty,apple,fruit-apple,Rome Beauty,Malus domestica Borkh.,Culinary / Dessert,"Originated with H.N. Gillett in Lawrence County, Ohio, USA. Brought to notice in 1848. Fruits have creamy white, rather coarse-textured, juicy flesh with very little flavour. Fruits do not mature well in the UK.",?Imperatore|?Morella|Beaute de Rome|Belle de Rome|Faust's Rome Beauty|Frumusetea Romei|Gillet's Seedling|Gillett's Seedling|Morgenduit|Mussolinieapfel|Pomme de Romagne|Rimskaia Krasavita|Rimskaya Krasavitsa|Rimske Krasne|Roma szepe|Roman Beauty|Rome|Rome's Beauty,Material available from the National Fruit Collection. Father to: Monroe Sports: Barkley Red Rome Double Red Rome Beauty Glengyle Red Red Rome Ruby Rome Beauty,True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=5428&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),5428,,05-19,05-25,,Mid October,21,,,,,,,,,,,,medium-large,Oblong,weak,,Whitish yellow,,Orange,striped,,,Greenish,61.50 mm,77.50 mm,soft,,
apple-winesap,apple,fruit-apple,Winesap,Malus domestica Borkh.,Culinary / Dessert,"Originated in the U.S.A. First described in 1817. Fruits have firm, tender, coarse, yellowish white flesh with a sweet, subacid flavour.",American Wine Sop|American Wine-Sop|American Winesop|Banana|Henrick's Sweet|Holland's Red Winter|Pot Pie Apple|Potpie Apple|Red Sweet Wine Sop|Royal Red|Royal Red of Kentucky|Texan Red|Wine Sap|Wine Sop|Winesop|Winter Winesap,Material available from the National Fruit Collection. Mother to: Arkansas Mareda McLiver's Winesap Shenandoah Sports: Dermen Winesap Accession No. 1951 - 103 fingerprint check_circle Accession name Winesap,True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=6820&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),6820,,05-10,05-18,,Late October,20,,,,,,,,,,,,medium,Globose conical,very weak,medium,Green yellow,,Red,striped,very low,,Yellowish,,,firm,,
apple-northern-spy,apple,fruit-apple,Northern Spy,Malus domestica Borkh.,Dessert,"First grown in the seedling orchard of Heman Chapin, at East Bloomfield, New York, USA from seed brought from Salisbury, Connecticut, USA. It was raised in about 1800 and introduced in 1840. Fruits have fairly firm, juicy, sweet flesh with a pleasant flavour. This variety is resistant to woolly aphis and has been used as a parent in the breeding of resistant rootstocks and varieties.",King Apple|King's Apple|Severnui Razvedchik|Severnui Shpion|Spaeher des Nordens|Spaher des Nordens|Spy,Material available from the National Fruit Collection. Material held in Tidnor Wood National Collection® of Malus (Cider making) Material held in the Marcher Apple Network collections (Paramor) Mother to: Sandow Sunrise Emilia Thurso Ascot Galton Glenton Spiza Father to: Pewaukee Ontario Sports: Crimson Spy Double Red Northern Spy Hunter Kinkead Spy Kinkead Red Spy Loop Spy,True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=4286&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),4286,,05-17,05-24,,Mid October,21,,,,,,,,,,,,large,Broad globose conical,weak-medium,,Green yellow,,Pink,,very low,,Yellowish,70.00 mm,81.00 mm,firm,,
apple-mutsu,apple,fruit-apple,Mutsu,Malus domestica Borkh.,Culinary / Dessert,"Triploid. Raised in Japan in 1930 and first fruited in 1939. It was named 'Mutsu' in 1948 but renamed 'Crispin' in the UK for commercial reasons in 1968. Fruits have firm, fine-textured, juicy flesh which is a little sweet, somewhat acid with a refreshing, and pleasant flavour.",Crispin,Material available from the National Fruit Collection.,True,,https://www.nationalfruitcollection.org.uk/full2.php?id=4148&&fruit=apple,Open Government Licence (Crown Copyright; excluding logos),4148,,05-10,05-17,,Mid October,20,,,,true,,,,,,,,large,Truncate conical,medium,,Green,,Brown,,,crisp,White,70.00 mm,70.00 mm,firm,,
